code_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/875261-mage-2e-char-sheets?p=892113#post892113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, the sheets have been updated, so re-download when you get a chance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you so much! Going to get these out to my players ASAP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T19:21:40-07:00","id":892198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/875261-mage-2e-char-sheets?p=892113#post892113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well....check boxes in Acrobat don't work that way sadly. It's basically an on/off, and then only one type of check.<br /> <br /> But, I did something similar to what I did for Exalted 3rd ed. I made the check boxes have a small type in field, so you can type in &quot;X&quot; or &quot;/&quot; or whatever. So check that out and see what you think. Hopefully that'll work for you. Best I can do, unless you want them to be fill in boxes...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's awesome, thank you very much <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11809-vilevader","name":"Vilevader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11809_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T21:52:23-07:00","id":892274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/875261-mage-2e-char-sheets?p=892174#post892174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I think Justin thought I was talking about Aspirations. But it's cool, blank lines are nice and versatile!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not totally on this, as I like my Char Sheets to remind me what I <b>do not</b> have right on them. Well, I can live without stating Nimbus sections, just like I can live with Spell Inures instead of Wisdom Inures...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T23:08:14-07:00","id":892318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/875261-mage-2e-char-sheets?p=892274#post892274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not totally on this, as I like my Char Sheets to remind me what I <b>do not</b> have right on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like having the section labels too, and I will probably ask Mr. Gone to add them back into the alternate version when he has the time to work on it. But for the time being, I concede that just blank lines without those labels is more versatile and as such should be the way it's done on the general sheet, because it will be more useful to more groups.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/875261-mage-2e-char-sheets?p=892274#post892274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I can live without stating Nimbus sections, just like I can live with Spell Inures instead of Wisdom Inures...</div> </div> </div> </div>Wyrd, Wisdom Inures doesn't make sense as a header for that section because Wisdom Inures aren't a thing in the book. Nor are Spell Inures for that matter, because the word Inure isn't a noun. It's a verb, meaning &quot;to desensitize&quot;. You don't have Inures (of any kind), you Inure Spells, which is why I asked Mr. Gone to change the name of the section to Inured Spells. That's what they're called in the book, and it's gramatically correct English.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T23:20:34-07:00","id":892329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/875261-mage-2e-char-sheets?p=892318#post892318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wyrd, Wisdom Inures doesn't make sense as a header for that section because Wisdom Inures aren't a thing in the book. Nor are Spell Inures for that matter, because the word Inure isn't a noun. It's a verb, meaning &quot;to desensitize&quot;. You don't have Inures (of any kind), you Inure Spells, which is why I asked Mr. Gone to change the name of the section to Inured Spells. That's what they're called in the book, and it's gramatically correct English.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not concern what is grammatical correct - I'm concern that Inures are in Wisdom section and are made to shield from Wisdom loss. Half of sheet is ungrammatical ( from what I know English ), they are called this terms to be mnemonics devises. I put higher utility and looking in correct section of corebook over English grammar correctness. But it's my opinion on matter only.<br /> <br /> And really? Yeah, if Inuring mean &quot;hardening&quot; in English, then you <i>are</i> hardening your Wisdom, not spells. Spells are amoral to traits, they do not flow with small particles of Wisdom to harden them. With Inuring you change slightly your private own Wisdom, so it's logical to call them &quot;Wisdom Inures&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-17-2016, 02:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T04:28:05-07:00","id":892418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/875261-mage-2e-char-sheets?p=892197#post892197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you so much! Going to get these out to my players ASAP.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're very welcome!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilevader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/875261-mage-2e-char-sheets?p=892198#post892198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's awesome, thank you very much <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>You're welcome! Glad you liked that idea. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/875261-mage-2e-char-sheets?p=892274#post892274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not totally on this, as I like my Char Sheets to remind me what I <b>do not</b> have right on them. Well, I can live without stating Nimbus sections, just like I can live with Spell Inures instead of Wisdom Inures...</div> </div> </div> </div>I wondered what you thought about that...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/875261-mage-2e-char-sheets?p=892318#post892318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like having the section labels too, and I will probably ask Mr. Gone to add them back into the alternate version when he has the time to work on it. But for the time being, I concede that just blank lines without those labels is more versatile and as such should be the way it's done on the general sheet, because it will be more useful to more groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. I don't mind labeling them a certain way and can totally do it. It just started to seem like everyone was getting a different idea on how it needed to labeled. If we can get a consensus, I have no issues changing it again...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/875261-mage-2e-char-sheets?p=892329#post892329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not concern what is grammatical correct - I'm concern that Inures are in Wisdom section and are made to shield from Wisdom loss. Half of sheet is ungrammatical ( from what I know English ), they are called this terms to be mnemonics devises. I put higher utility and looking in correct section of corebook over English grammar correctness. But it's my opinion on matter only.<br /> <br /> And really? Yeah, if Inuring mean &quot;hardening&quot; in English, then you <i>are</i> hardening your Wisdom, not spells. Spells are amoral to traits, they do not flow with small particles of Wisdom to harden them. With Inuring you change slightly your private own Wisdom, so it's logical to call them &quot;Wisdom Inures&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well....if y'all get that worked out, let me know and I can change it to whatever.<br /> <br /> Or, I can make that an interactive header and people can type in whatever they need it to be. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T08:07:35-07:00","id":892519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/875261-mage-2e-char-sheets?p=892329#post892329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not concern what is grammatical correct - I'm concern that Inures are in Wisdom section and are made to shield from Wisdom loss. Half of sheet is ungrammatical ( from what I know English ), they are called this terms to be mnemonics devises. I put higher utility and looking in correct section of corebook over English grammar correctness. But it's my opinion on matter only.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the rest of the sheet is gramatically correct. It's not complete sentences, but the words are all the proper parts of speech, which &quot;Inures&quot; is not, because Inures aren't things, Inuring is something you do. You wouldn't change Controled Spells to &quot;Gnosis Controls&quot; because that's not what they're called and it doesn't make sense. The same should be true of changing Inured Spells to &quot;Wisdom Inures&quot;. If you want the label to be functional, it makes more sense to call it what it's actually called in the book and just use the Index.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/875261-mage-2e-char-sheets?p=892329#post892329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And really? Yeah, if Inuring mean &amp;quot;hardening&amp;quot; in English, then you <i>are</i> hardening your Wisdom, not spells. Spells are amoral to traits, they do not flow with small particles of Wisdom to harden them. With Inuring you change slightly your private own Wisdom, so it's logical to call them &amp;quot;Wisdom Inures&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're hardening yourself to the spell. Here's what the book says about Inuring:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If a mage suffers Wisdom loss through use of a spell, she can choose to wipe that spell from future Acts of Hubris; any future uses will not incur Wisdom loss no matter the action. If she chooses to do this, to inure herself to the spell\u2019s hubris, it forever becomes a Paradox risk. From that point forward, every use of the <b>inured spell</b> forces a base two-die Paradox risk. Your character may inure herself to the effects of one spell per dot of her Gnosis. </div> </div> </div>Here, the phrase &quot;Inured Spell&quot; is being used, correctly, to mean &quot;spell against which you are Inured&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T08:41:48-07:00","id":892545,"title":"","content":"I checked my corebook file and it's says:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MtAw 2E, p.88</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Inuring </b><br /> If a mage suffers Wisdom loss through use of a spell, she can choose to wipe that spell from future Acts of Hubris; any future uses will not incur Wisdom loss no matter the action. If she chooses to do this, to inure herself to the spell\u2019s hubris, it forever becomes a Paradox risk. From that point forward, every use of the inured spell forces a base two-die Paradox risk. Your character may inure herself to the effects of one spell per dot of her Gnosis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Inuring is done <i>on Wisdom</i>, not the spells themselves. You are not Inuring spells, only part of you Wisdom that is responsible for Acts of Hubris on them.<br /> <br /> In my dictionary, it means that term for section should be <b>Wisdom Inuring</b>, simple.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/875261-mage-2e-char-sheets?p=892418#post892418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, I can make that an interactive header and people can type in whatever they need it to be. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It won't be necessary - one of us have right. Other can live with other name on the section on sheet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-17-2016, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T09:09:52-07:00","id":892566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/875261-mage-2e-char-sheets?p=892545#post892545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I checked my corebook file and it's says:</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's the exact section I just quoted, and if you read it again more carefully, you'll notice that it contains the phrase &quot;Inured Spells&quot;, which it uses (correctly) to mean &quot;spells to which you are inured&quot; as I just pointed out in my previous post. You'll also note that it does not contain the phrase Wisdom Inures or Wisdom Inuring.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/875261-mage-2e-char-sheets?p=892545#post892545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Inuring is done <i>on Wisdom</i>, not the spells themselves. You are not Inuring spells, only part of you Wisdom that is responsible for Acts of Hubris on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you are Inuring yourself to the spell's Hubris. It literally says those exact words, right there in the section we both quoted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/875261-mage-2e-char-sheets?p=892545#post892545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my dictionary, it means that term for section should be <b>Wisdom Inuring</b>, simple.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then your dictionary is wrong. The quote quite clearly says the words &quot;Inured Spells&quot;, the simple thing to do is to call the section the same thing the book calls it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T10:55:33-07:00","id":892629,"title":"","content":"Hey Wyrd, how about trusting the native English speaker that she knows how the language works?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T11:14:22-07:00","id":894181,"title":"","content":"Oh my gosh Mr. Gone the new sheet is so great! I'm so glad you moved familiar to page 3, that was such a good decision! I love the new sheets. :3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T17:35:00-07:00","id":894462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <